# TypeScript and React clients

Follow `docs/engineering/development-standards.md` and
`docs/engineering/testing-quality-gates.md`.

- Keep strict TypeScript enabled and avoid `any`.
- Run ESLint, Prettier, type checking, tests, and production builds.
- Use `const` by default, strict equality, immutable inputs/state, and
  validated external payloads.
- Keep components and hooks pure during render. Follow the Rules of Hooks and
  clean up effects, subscriptions, listeners, timers, and in-flight work.
- Use typed props; do not add PropTypes.
- Keep authentication secrets out of browser storage and general mobile
  storage. Mobile refresh credentials belong only in Keychain/Keystore.
- Never make authorization decisions in a client.
- Preserve keyboard, screen-reader, focus, contrast, touch-target, and
  reduced-motion accessibility.
- Do not render unsanitized HTML or persist protected page imagery.
- Test loading, empty, offline, retry, forbidden, expired, revoked, and
  processing states.
